    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>An Ionian island state off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#asia-minor">Asia Minor</a>, settled c. 1000 BCE, that became one of the richest cities in the Greek world.</li><li>Its wine, mastic and fleet made it a leading member of the Ionian League and, later, an autonomous naval ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#athens">Athens</a>.</li><li>Chios had early popular institutions and, by ancient accounts, more slaves than any Greek state except <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#sparta">Sparta</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#herodotus">Herodotus</a> credits Glaucus of Chios with inventing the welding of iron; he made a famous iron stand for a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#silver">silver</a> bowl dedicated at Delphi by Alyattes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#lydia">Lydia</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

